<https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2001/19/eng@/~part_VI__cl_37> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://docs.oasis-open.org/legaldocml/ns/akn/3.0#clause> <https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2001/19/eng@> .
<https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2001/19/eng@/~part_VI__cl_37> <https://schema.org/text> "A legal officer as defined in the Government Proceedings Act 1956 [Act 359] or a legal officer of the Commission who has been admitted as an advocate and solicitor under the Legal Profession Act 1976 may appear in any civil proceedings involving the Commission or any person holding any of the offices specified in the Second Schedule in the performance of his functions under any written law specified in the First Schedule and may make and do all acts and applications in respect of such proceedings on behalf of the Commission or such person, as the case may be. Obligation of secrecy"@en <https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2001/19/eng@> .
